/*  Input and output — files, directories, paths, streams, running programs and subprocess pipes,
    the environment. From `TypeChecker.Failures.cs`, `TypeChecker.Pipes.cs` and the smaller arms of
    `TypeChecker.Core.cs`.

    ★ Reading a file, listing a directory and running a program can each FAIL, and are handled the
    way a fallible call is: inside a `Try` the value is the success, under `but on failure` or `or
    pass the failure off` it is the `… or failure`, and anywhere else it is refused. Writing, making
    and removing are fallible STATEMENTS instead — an enclosing `Try` catches them, and nothing is
    asked of the line itself.

    ⚠ A pipe of FUNCTIONS is in `tasks.cufe`: its stages' bodies are checked again with what flows
    into them.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// What reading, listing or running gives back, in the context it stands in.
    Bind node or failure to fallible-result unto checker, given (the node success, the text context, the number at-row,
            the text action, the text fix):
        If one's in-try, return success.
        If one's handled is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (context, "", at-row, action, fix)).
        Done.
        Return cast wrapped on ("FailureType", success).
    Done.

    /// `(errors: text, exit-code: number, output: text)` — what a `run` gives back.
    Bind node to run-result-type:
        Define named as cast listed.
        For each pair in a series with ("errors", "exit-code", "output"), repeat:
            Define field as cast listed.
            Cast field's add on (cast quoted on (pair)).
            If pair is "exit-code", cast field's add on (cast plain-type on ("NumberType")).
            Otherwise, cast field's add on (cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
            Cast named's add on (field).
        Done.
        Return cast made on ("RecordType", a series with (cast listed, named)).
    Done.

    // ── Files, directories, paths ─────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `read all [lines] from the file <path>`.
    Bind node or failure to infer-file-read unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define path-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (path-type, "TextType", "a file path must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (path-type)} as a file path",
            "Write the path as a text literal like \"config.txt\", or use a text variable.") or pass the failure off.
        Define success as cast plain-type on ("TextType").
        If (cast field-of on (said, 1))'s word is "AllLines", the success becomes cast wrapped on ("SeriesType", cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
        Return cast one's fallible-result on (success, "reading from a file can fail — you must handle the failure", at-row,
            "use a file read's result without handling the failure",
            "Wrap the read in a 'Try to: / In case of failure:' block, use 'but on failure <default>', or use 'or pass the failure off'.") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `the contents of the directory <path>`.
    Bind node or failure to infer-directory-contents unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
        Define path-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (path-type, "TextType", "a directory path must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (path-type)} as a directory path",
            "Write the path as a text literal like \"/home/user\", or use a text variable.") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast one's fallible-result on (cast wrapped on ("SeriesType", cast plain-type on ("TextType")),
            "listing a directory can fail — you must handle the failure", at-row,
            "use a directory listing's result without handling the failure",
            "Wrap it in a 'Try to: / In case of failure:' block, use 'but on failure <default>', or use 'or pass the failure off'.") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `the path <path> exists | is a directory | is a file` — never fails.
    Bind node or failure to infer-path-check unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define path-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (path-type, "TextType", "a path must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (path-type)} as a path", "Write the path as a text literal, or use a text variable.") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast plain-type on ("FactType").
    Done.

    /// `Make the directory …`, `Remove the file …`, `Remove the directory …`.
    Bind void or failure to check-path-action unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Define path-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (path-type, "TextType", "a path must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (path-type)} as a path",
            "Write the path as a text literal like \"books\", or use a text variable.") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `The current directory becomes <path>.`
    Bind void or failure to check-directory-set unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
        Define path-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (path-type, "TextType", "a directory path must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (path-type)} as a directory path",
            "The path must be a text expression (a string literal or a text variable).") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `Write|Append <text> to the file <path>.`
    Bind void or failure to check-file-write unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define value-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (value-type, "TextType", "you can only write text to a file", at-row,
            "write a {cast type-words on (value-type)} to a file",
            "Convert the value to text first with 'converted to text', or build a text value with 'joined to'.") or pass the failure off.
        Define path-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (path-type, "TextType", "a file path must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (path-type)} as a file path",
            "Write the path as a text literal like \"output.txt\", or use a text variable.") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    // ── Streams ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `With the file <path> open for reading|writing as <name>: … Done.`
    /// ⚠ Its statements are checked one by one, not as a block — so a guard inside narrows nothing
    /// for the statements after it. That is C#'s `CheckWithOpen`, copied as it is.
    Bind void or failure to check-with-open unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 5)).
        Define at-column as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 6)).
        Define path-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (path-type, "TextType", "a file path must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (path-type)} as a file path",
            "Write the path as a text literal like \"data.txt\", or use a text variable.") or pass the failure off.
        Define stream-kind as "WritableStreamType".
        If (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s word is "Reading", the stream-kind becomes "ReadableStreamType".
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Cast one's enter-scope.
        Cast one's bind-name on (name, a new binding {
            the shape cast wrapped on (stream-kind, cast plain-type on ("TextType")),
            the established-by cast placed-reference on (name, at-row, at-column),
            the line at-row, the permanent false, the module false, the depth 0, the parameter false }).
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
            Cast one's check-statement on (inner) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast one's exit-scope.
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-text-stream, given (the node shape, the text stream-kind):
        Return shape's kind is stream-kind and (cast field-of on (shape, 1))'s kind is "TextType".
    Done.

    /// `Write <text> to <stream>.`
    Bind void or failure to check-stream-write unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Define value-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (value-type, "TextType", "you can only write text to a stream", at-row,
            "write a {cast type-words on (value-type)} to a stream",
            "Convert the value to text first with 'converted to text', or build a text value with 'joined to'.") or pass the failure off.
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define target-type as cast one's infer on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-none on (target-type), return.
        // Writing to TEXT is a file name missing `the file`.
        If target-type's kind is "TextType":
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("you can write to a file or a stream, and this is a piece of text", "", at-row,
                "write to {cast expression-words on (target)}",
                "If it names a file, say so: 'Write … to the file {cast expression-words on (target)}.'")).
        Done.
        If cast is-text-stream on (target-type, "WritableStreamType"), return.
        If cast beyond-types on (target-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("writing to a {target-type's kind}")).
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("write expects a writable stream of text", "", at-row,
            "write to a {cast type-words on (target-type)}",
            "Use a writable stream — open a file 'for writing' with 'With the file ... open for writing as s:'.")).
    Done.

    /// `read a line | all | all lines from <stream>`.
    Bind node or failure to infer-read unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define form as (cast field-of on (said, 1))'s word.
        Define source as cast field-of on (said, 2).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define source-type as cast one's infer on (source) or pass the failure off.
        // Reading from TEXT is nearly always a file name missing its two words.
        If source-type's kind is "TextType" and (form is "All" or form is "AllLines"):
            Define spoken-form as "all".
            If form is "AllLines", the spoken-form becomes "all lines".
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("you can read from a file or a stream, and this is a piece of text", "", at-row,
                "read from {cast expression-words on (source)}",
                "If it names a file, say so: 'read {spoken-form} from the file {cast expression-words on (source)}'.")).
        Done.
        If cast is-none on (source-type) is false and cast is-text-stream on (source-type, "ReadableStreamType") is false:
            If cast beyond-types on (source-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("reading from a {source-type's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("read expects a readable stream of text", "", at-row,
                "read from a {cast type-words on (source-type)}",
                "Use a readable stream of text as the source — 'the input' is always available, or use 'With the file ... open for reading as s:' for a file stream.")).
        Done.
        If form is "Line", return cast wrapped on ("VoidableType", cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
        If form is "AllLines", return cast wrapped on ("SeriesType", cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
        Return cast plain-type on ("TextType").
    Done.

    // ── Running programs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The argument half both `run` forms share — `CheckRunArguments`.
    Bind void or failure to check-run-arguments unto checker, given (the node listed-args, the node args-series,
            the number at-row):
        If cast is-nothing on (args-series) is false:
            Define series-type as cast one's infer on (args-series) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (series-type), return.
            If series-type's kind is "SeriesType" and (cast field-of on (series-type, 1))'s kind is "TextType", return.
            If cast beyond-types on (series-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("arguments of a {series-type's kind}")).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the arguments must be a series of text", "", at-row,
                "use a {cast type-words on (series-type)} as a program’s argument list",
                "Every argument crosses to the program as a separate text value, so the list must be a series of text.")).
        Done.
        Define count as the number of listed-args's children.
        For each argument in listed-args's children, repeat:
            Define argument-type as cast one's infer on (argument) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (argument-type) is false and argument-type's kind is not "TextType":
                If count is 1 and argument-type's kind is "SeriesType" and (cast field-of on (argument-type, 1))'s kind is "TextType":
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the parentheses make this one argument, not the whole argument list", "",
                        at-row, "pass a series of text inside the parentheses",
                        "Write 'with arguments <the series>' with no parentheses to pass the whole list, or 'with arguments (<one>, <two>)' to write the arguments out.")).
                Done.
                If cast beyond-types on (argument-type), return a failure (cast not-judged on ("an argument of a {argument-type's kind}")).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("each argument must be text", "", at-row,
                    "use a {cast type-words on (argument-type)} as a program argument",
                    "Arguments are passed directly to the program — each must be a text value.")).
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `run <program> [with arguments …] [with the terminal] [with input <text>]`.
    Bind node or failure to infer-run unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 4)).
        Define program-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (program-type, "TextType", "the program to run must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (program-type)} as the program name",
            "Write the program name as a text literal like \"ls\", or use a text variable.") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's check-run-arguments on (cast field-of on (said, 2), cast field-of on (said, 3), at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Define fed as cast field-of on (said, 7).
        If cast is-nothing on (fed) is false:
            If cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (said, 6)):
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("a run cannot say both 'with the terminal' and 'with input'", "", at-row,
                    "give the child the keyboard and type for it at the same time",
                    "'with the terminal' hands the child the real keyboard; 'with input' feeds it text instead. Drop 'with the terminal' to feed it, or drop 'with input' to let someone type.")).
            Done.
            Define fed-type as cast one's infer on (fed) or pass the failure off.
            Cast require-kind on (fed-type, "TextType", "the input fed to a program must be text", at-row,
                "feed a {cast type-words on (fed-type)} to a program",
                "A child reads bytes, so 'with input' takes text. Convert it first if you have something else.") or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Return cast one's fallible-result on (cast run-result-type, "running a program can fail — you must handle the failure", at-row,
            "use a run result without handling the launch failure",
            "Wrap in 'Try to: / In case of failure:', use 'but on failure <default>', or use 'or pass the failure off'.") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `Run <program> [with arguments …].` — for its effect; the launch can still fail.
    Bind void or failure to check-run-statement unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        Define program-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (program-type, "TextType", "the program to run must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (program-type)} as the program name",
            "Write the program name as a text literal like \"vim\", or use a text variable.") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's check-run-arguments on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), cast field-of on (statement, 3), at-row) or pass the failure off.
        If one's in-try or one's handled, return.
        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("running a program can fail — you must handle the failure", "", at-row,
            "run a program without handling the launch failure", "Wrap it in 'Try to: / In case of failure:'.")).
    Done.

    // ── Pipes of programs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `A | B | C`, left to right.
    Bind void to gather-stages, given (the node said, the series of node stages):
        If said's kind is "PipeExpression":
            Cast gather-stages on (cast field-of on (said, 1), stages).
            Cast gather-stages on (cast field-of on (said, 2), stages).
            Return.
        Done.
        Insert said into stages.
    Done.

    Bind series of node to pipe-stages, given (the node said):
        Define stages as a series of node.
        Cast gather-stages on (said, stages).
        Return stages.
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-program-pipe, given (the node said):
        For each stage in cast pipe-stages on (said), repeat:
            If stage's kind is not "RunExpression", return false.
        Done.
        Return true.
    Done.

    /// A stage that hands its output to the terminal, or is fed while a stage before feeds it.
    /// ⚠ Bare messages, not the four-part form — C# throws these as they are.
    Bind void or failure to refuse-terminal-in-pipe, given (the series of node stages):
        For each stage in stages, repeat:
            If stage's kind is "RunExpression" and cast truth-of on (cast field-of on (stage, 6)):
                Return a failure "error\ta run in a pipe cannot say 'with the terminal' — a pipe carries the program's output to the next stage, and 'with the terminal' sends it to the screen instead. Drop 'with the terminal' to pipe it, or run it on its own to watch it.".
            Done.
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each stage in stages, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If place is greater than 1 and stage's kind is "RunExpression" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (stage, 7)) is false:
                Return a failure "error\tonly the first stage of a pipe can say 'with input' — every later stage is already fed by the one before it, and a program has only one stdin.".
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Each stage's program and arguments, with the launch failure waived per stage.
    Bind void or failure to check-pipe-stages unto checker, given (the series of node stages):
        Define earlier as one's handled.
        The one's handled becomes true.
        For each stage in stages, repeat:
            Try to:
                Cast one's infer on (stage).
            Done.
            In case of failure:
                The one's handled becomes earlier.
                Return a failure (the message of the failure).
            Done.
        Done.
        The one's handled becomes earlier.
    Done.

    /// `run A | run B` as a statement — fire and wait.
    Bind void or failure to check-pipe-statement unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define stages as cast pipe-stages on (said).
        Cast refuse-terminal-in-pipe on (stages) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-program-pipe on (said) is false:
            Cast one's check-task-pipe on (stages) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        Cast one's check-pipe-stages on (stages) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `run A | run B` as a value — what one `run` gives back, in the same context.
    Bind node or failure to infer-pipe unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 3)).
        Define stages as cast pipe-stages on (said).
        Cast refuse-terminal-in-pipe on (stages) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-program-pipe on (said) is false:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("only subprocess pipes can be used as values", "", at-row,
                "use a task-function pipe in expression position",
                "Task pipes are statement-only. Only 'run A | run B' subprocess pipes produce a result record.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-pipe-stages on (stages) or pass the failure off.
        Return cast one's fallible-result on (cast run-result-type, "running a program can fail — you must handle the failure", at-row,
            "use a subprocess pipe without handling the launch failure",
            "Wrap in 'Try to: / In case of failure:', use 'but on failure <default>', or use 'or pass the failure off'.") or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    // ── The environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `the environment variable <name>` — void when it is not set.
    Bind node or failure to infer-env-var unto checker, given (the node said):
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (said, 2)).
        Define name-type as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (said, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast require-kind on (name-type, "TextType", "the environment variable name must be text", at-row,
            "use a {cast type-words on (name-type)} as an environment variable name",
            "The variable name must be a text expression (a string literal or a text variable).") or pass the failure off.
        Return cast wrapped on ("VoidableType", cast plain-type on ("TextType")).
    Done.
Done.
